{
  "title": "45: al-Jaaseyah الجاثية",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nحٰمٓ‌‌ ۚ‏(1)\nHAA-MEEM.\nHa-Mim. \nتَنْزِيْلُ الْكِتٰبِ مِنَ اللّٰهِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَكِيْمِ‏(2)\nTANZEELU KETAABE MENAL LAAHE A’ZEEZIL HAKEEM.\nThe revelation of the Book is from Allah the Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom. \nاِنَّ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَؕ‏(3)\nINNAL FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE LA-AAYAATIL LLELMUMENEENA.\nVerily in the heavens and the earth, are Signs for those who believe. \nوَفِىْ خَلْقِكُمْ وَمَا يَبُثُّ مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَۙ‏(4)\nWA FEE KHALQEKUM WA MAA YABUSSU MIN DAAAB-BATIL AAYAATUM LEQAWMINY YOOQENOON.\nAnd in the creation of yourselves and the fact that animals are scattered (through the earth), are Signs for those of assured Faith. \nوَاخْتِلَافِ الَّيْلِ وَالنَّهَارِ وَمَاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مِنْ رِّزْقٍ فَاَحْيَا بِهِ الْاَرْضَ بَعْدَ مَوْتِهَا وَ تَصْرِيْفِ الرِّيٰحِ اٰيٰتٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّعْقِلُوْنَ‏(5)\nWAKHTELAAFIL LAYLE WAN NAHAARE WA MAA ANZALAL LAAHO MENAL SAMAAA-E MIN RREZQIN FA-AHYAA BEHIL ARZA BA’DA MAWTEHAA WA TASREEFE REYAAHE AAYAATUM LEQAWMINY YA’QELOON.\nAnd in the alternation of Night and Day, and the fact that Allah sends down Sustenance from the sky, and revives therewith the earth after its death, and in the change of the winds, are Signs for those that are wise. \nتِلْكَ اٰيٰتُ اللّٰهِ نَتْلُوْهَا عَلَيْكَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ‌ۚ فَبِاَىِّ حَدِيْثٍۢ بَعْدَ اللّٰهِ وَاٰيٰتِهٖ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(6)\nTILKA AAYAATUL LAAHE NATLOOHAA A’LAYKA BIL-HAQQE FABE-AYYE HADEESIN BA’DA LAAHE WA AAYAATEHI YOAMENOONA.\nSuch are the Signs of Allah, which We rehearse to thee in Truth; then in what exposition will they believe after (rejecting) Allah and His Signs? \nوَيْلٌ لِّكُلِّ اَفَّاكٍ اَثِيْمٍۙ‏(7)\nWAYLUL LEKULLE AAFFAAKIN ASEEM.\nWoe to each sinful dealer in Falsehoods: \nيَّسْمَعُ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِ ثُمَّ يُصِرُّ مُسْتَكْبِرًا كَاَنْ لَّمْ يَسْمَعْهَا‌ ۚ فَبَشِّرْهُ بِعَذَابٍ اَ لِيْمٍ‏(8)\nYYASMAU’U AAYAATIL LAAHE TUTLAA A’LAYHE SUMMA YUSERRU MUSTAKBERAN KA-AN LAM YASMAA’HAA BE BE-A’ZAABIN ALEEM.\nHe hears the Signs of Allah rehearsed to him, yet is obstinate and lofty, as if he had not heard them: then announce to him a Penalty Grievous! \nوَاِذَا عَلِمَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا شَيْئًا اۨتَّخَذَهَا هُزُوًا‌ ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مُّهِيْنٌ ؕ‏(9)\nWA EZAA A’LEMA MIN AAYAATENAA SHAY-ANW ATTAKHAZAHAA HOZOWANW OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MOHEEN.\nAnd when he learns something of Our Signs, he takes them in jest: for such there will be a humiliating Penalty. \nمِنْ وَّرَآئِهِمْ جَهَنَّمُۚ وَلَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَسَبُوْا شَيْئًا وَّلَا مَا اتَّخَذُوْا مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْلِيَآءَ‌ ۚ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ عَظِيْمٌؕ‏(10)\nMIN WA-RAAA-EHIM JAHANNAMUL WA LAA YUGHNEE A’NHUM MAA KASABOO SHAY-ANW WA LAA MAA ATTAKHAZOOA MIN DOONIL LAAHE AAWLEEAAAA WA LAHUM A’ZAABUN A’AZEEMUN.\nIn front of them is Hell: and of no profit to them is anything they may have earned, nor any protectors they may have taken to themselves besides Allah: for them is a tremendous Penalty. \nهٰذَا هُدًى‌ ‌ۚ وَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّنْ رِّجْزٍ اَلِيْمٌ‏(11)\nHAAZAA HODAM WAL LAZEENA KAFAROO BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM LAHUM A’ZAABUN MIN RREJZIN ALEEM.\nThis is (true) Guidance and for those who reject the Signs of their Lord, is a grievous Penalty of abomination. \nاَللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ سَخَّرَ لَكُمُ الْبَحْرَ لِتَجْرِىَ الْفُلْكُ فِيْهِ بِاَمْرِهٖ وَلِتَبْتَغُوْا مِنْ فَضْلِهٖ وَلَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ‌ۚ‏(12)\nALLAAHO LAZEE SAKKHARA LAKOMUL BAHRA LETAJREAAA FULKO FEEHE LAAHO WA LETABTAGHOO MIN FAZLEHI WA LA-A’LLAKUM TASHKOROON.\nIt is Allah Who has subjected the sea to you, that ships may sail through it by His command, that ye may seek of his Bounty, and that ye may be grateful. \nوَسَخَّرَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ جَمِيْعًا مِّنْهُ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّقَوْمٍ يَّتَفَكَّرُوْنَ‏(13)\nSAKHKHARASH LAKUM MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE JAMEE-A’A MINHO INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEQAWMINY YATAFAKKAROON.\nAnd He has subjected to you, as from Him, all that is in the heavens and on earth: Behold, in that are Signs indeed for those who reflect. \nقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا يَغْفِرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ لَا يَرْجُوْنَ اَيَّامَ اللّٰهِ لِيَجْزِىَ قَوْمًۢا بِمَا كَانُوْا يَكْسِبُوْنَ‏(14)\nQUL LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO YAGHFEROOA LILLAZEENA LAA YARJOON AAYAMA LAAHE LE-YAJZEYAL QAWMAN BEMAA KAANOO YAKSEBOON.\nTell those who believe, to forgive those who do not look forward to the Days of Allah: It is for Him to recompense (for good or ill) each People according to what they have earned. \nمَنْ عَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَلِنَفْسِهٖ‌ۚ وَمَنْ اَسَآءَ فَعَلَيْهَا ثُمَّ اِلٰى رَبِّكُمْ تُرْجَعُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN A’MELA SAALEHAN FALENAFSEH WA MAN ASAAA-A FA A’LAYHAA SUMMA ELAA RABBEKUM TURJA-O’ON.\nIf any one does a righteous deed, it ensures to the benefit of his own soul; if he does evil, it works against (his own soul). In the end will ye (all) be brought back to your Lord. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ الْكِتٰبَ وَالْحُكْمَ وَالنُّبُوَّةَ وَرَزَقْنٰهُمْ مِّنَ الطَّيِّبٰتِ وَفَضَّلْنٰهُمْ عَلَى الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‌ۚ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ KETAABA WAL HUKMA WA NOBUWWATA WA RAZAQNAAHUM MENAL AT-TAYBAATE WAFAZZALNAAHUM A’LAL A’ALAMEEN.\nWe did aforetime grant to the Children of Israel the Book the Power of Command, and Prophethood; We gave them, for Sustenance, things good and pure; and We favoured them above the nations. \nوَاٰتَيْنٰهُمْ بَيِّنٰتٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ‌ ۚ فَمَا اخْتَلَفُوْۤا اِلَّا مِنْۢ بَعْدِ مَا جَآءَهُمُ الْعِلْمُ ۙ بَغْيًاۢ بَيْنَهُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ يَقْضِىْ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فِيْمَا كَانُوْا فِيْهِ يَخْتَلِفُوْنَ‏(17)\nWA AATAYNAAHUM BAYYENAAT MENAL AL-AAMRE FAMAA TALAFOO ILLAA MIN BA’DE MAA JAAA-AHOMUL I’LMO BAGHYAN BAYNAHUM INNAL RABBAKA YAQZEE BAYNAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE FEEMAA KAANOO FEEHE YAKHTALEFOON.\nAnd We granted them Clear Signs in affairs (of Religion): it was only after knowledge had been granted to them that they fell into schisms, through insolent envy among themselves. Verily thy Lord will judge between them on the Day of Judgment as to those matters in which they set up differences. \nثُمَّ جَعَلْنٰكَ عَلٰى شَرِيْعَةٍ مِّنَ الْاَمْرِ فَاتَّبِعْهَا وَلَا تَتَّبِعْ اَهْوَآءَ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(18)\nSUMMA JAA’ALNAAKA A’LAA SHAREEA’ATIN MENAL AL-AAMRE FAATTABEA’HAA WA LAA TATTABEA’ AAHWAAA LAZEENA LAA YA’LAMOON.\nThen We put thee on the (right) Way of Religion: so follow thou that (Way), and follow not the desires of those who know not. \nاِنَّهُمْ لَنْ يُّغْنُوْا عَنْكَ مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا‌ ؕ وَ اِنَّ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بَعْضُهُمْ اَوْلِيَآءُ بَعْضٍ‌ ۚ وَاللّٰهُ وَلِىُّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(19)\nINNAHUM LAN YYUGHNOOA A’NKAL MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WA INNAL ZAALEMEEN KHALAA ANNAKUM AWLEYAAA-O ELAA WAL LAAHO WALIYYUL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN.\nThey will be of no use to thee in the sight of Allah: it is only Wrong-doers (that stand as) protectors, one to another: but Allah is the Protector of the Righteous. \nهٰذَا بَصَائِرُ لِلنَّاسِ وَهُدًى وَّرَحْمَةٌ لِّقَوْمٍ يُّوْقِنُوْنَ‏(20)\nHAAZAA BASAAERU LIN-NAASE WA HODANW WA RAHMATUL LEQAWMINY YOOQENOON.\nThese are clear evidences to men and a Guidance and Mercy to those of assured Faith. \nاَمْ حَسِبَ الَّذِيْنَ اجْتَرَحُوا السَّيِّاٰتِ اَنْ نَّجْعَلَهُمْ كَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ ۙ سَوَآءً مَّحْيَاهُمْ وَمَمَاتُهُمْ‌ ؕ سَآءَ مَا يَحْكُمُوْنَ‏(21)\nAM HASEBA LAZEENA AJTARAHOOA SAYYE-AATE AN NNAJA’ALAHUM TAKOONOO AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE SAWAAAN MMAHYAAHUM WAMAMAATUHUM SAAA-A MAA YAHKUMOONA.\nWhat! Do those who seek after evil ways think that We shall hold them equal with those who believe and do righteous deeds, that equal will be their life and their death? Ill is the judgment that they make. \nوَ خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ بِالْحَقِّ وَلِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتْ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ‏(22)\nWA KHALAQAL LAAHO SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BIL-HAQQE WALETUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA KASABAT WA HUM LAA LAA YUZLAMOON.\nAllah created the heavens and the earth for just ends, and in order that each soul may find the recompense of what it has earned, and none of them be wronged. \nاَفَرَءَيْتَ مَنِ اتَّخَذَ اِلٰهَهٗ هَوٰٮهُ وَاَضَلَّهُ اللّٰهُ عَلٰى عِلْمٍ وَّخَتَمَ عَلٰى سَمْعِهٖ وَقَلْبِهٖ وَجَعَلَ عَلٰى بَصَرِهٖ غِشٰوَةً  ؕ فَمَنْ يَّهْدِيْهِ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ اللّٰهِ‌ ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(23)\nAAFARAAYTA MANIS TAKHAZA AELAAHAH HAWHU WAAZALLAHU LAAHO A’LAA I’LMIN WWAKHATAMA A’LAA SAME’EH WA QALBEHI WA A’LAA BASAREH GHESHAAWATAN FAMAN YYAHDEEHE MIN BA’DE LAAHE AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThen seest thou such a one as takes as his god his own vain desire? Allah has, knowing (him as such), left him astray, and sealed his hearing and his heart (and understanding), and put a cover on his sight. Who, then, will guide him after Allah (has withdrawn Guidance)? Will ye not then receive admonition? \nوَقَالُوْا مَا هِىَ اِلَّا حَيَاتُنَا الدُّنْيَا نَمُوْتُ وَنَحْيَا وَمَا يُهْلِكُنَاۤ اِلَّا الدَّهْرُ‌ؕ وَمَا لَهُمْ بِذٰلِكَ مِنْ عِلْمٍ‌ ۚ اِنْ هُمْ اِلَّا يَظُنُّوْنَ‏(24)\nWA QAALOO MAA HEYA ILLAA HAYAATUNAA DUNYAA NAMOOTU WANAHYAA WA MAA YUHLEKUNAA ILLAA AD-DAHRU WA MAA LAHUM BE-ZAALEKA MIN I’LMIN IN HUM ILLAA YAZUNNOONA.\nAnd they say: “What is there but our life in this world? We shall die and we live, and nothing but time can destroy us.” But of that they have no knowledge: they merely conjecture: \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ مَّا كَانَ حُجَّتَهُمْ اِلَّاۤ اَنْ قَالُوا ائْتُوْا بِاٰبَآئِنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(25)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT MAA KAANA HUJJATAHUM ILLAA AN QAALUD ATOOA BE-AABAAA-ENAA IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nAnd when Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them their argument is nothing but this: They say, “Bring (back) our forefathers, if what ye say is true!” \nقُلِ اللّٰهُ يُحْيِيْكُمْ ثُمَّ يُمِيْتُكُمْ ثُمَّ يَجْمَعُكُمْ اِلٰى يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهِ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(26)\nQOLIL LAAHO YOHYEEKUM SUMMA YOMEETOKUM SUMMA YAJMAU’UKUM ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE LAA RAYBA FEEHE LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSay: “It is Allah Who gives you life, then gives you death; then He will gather you together for the Day of Judgment about which there is no doubt”: But most men do not understand. \nوَلِلّٰهِ مُلْكُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ؕ وَيَوْمَ تَقُوْمُ السَّاعَةُ يَوْمَئِذٍ يَّخْسَرُ الْمُبْطِلُوْنَ‏(27)\nLILLAAHE MULKUS SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ WA YAWMA YAQOOMUS SAA-A’TO YAWMA-EZIN YYAKHSARU MUBTELOON.\nTo Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth, and the Day that the Hour of Judgment is established, that Day will the dealers in Falsehood perish! \nوَتَرٰى كُلَّ اُمَّةٍ جَاثِيَةً‌ كُلُّ اُمَّةٍ تُدْعٰۤى اِلٰى كِتٰبِهَا ؕ اَلْيَوْمَ تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(28)\nWATARAA KULLA UMMATIN JAASEETAN KULLO UMMATIN TUDA’AA ELAA KETAABEHAA AL-YAWMA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\nAnd thou wilt see every sect bowing the knee: Every sect will be called to its Record: “This Day shall ye be recompensed for all that ye did! \nهٰذَا كِتٰبُنَا يَنْطِقُ عَلَيْكُمْ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ اِنَّا كُنَّا نَسْتَنْسِخُ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nHAAZAA KETAABUNAA YANTEQU A’LAYKUM BIL-HAQ INNAA KUNNAA NASTANSEKHU MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n“This Our Record speaks about you with truth: For We were wont to put on Record all that ye did.” \nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَيُدْخِلُهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ فِىْ رَحْمَتِهٖ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ هُوَ الْفَوْزُ الْمُبِيْنُ‏(30)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE FAYUDKHELUHUM RABBOHUM FEE FEE ZAA LEKA HOWA FAWZUL MOBEEN.\nThen, as to those who believed and did righteous deeds, their Lord will admit them to His Mercy that will be the achievement for all to see. \nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اَفَلَمْ تَكُنْ اٰيٰتِىْ تُتْلٰى عَلَيْكُمْ فَاسْتَكْبَرْتُمْ وَكُنْتُمْ قَوْمًا مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA KAFAROO A-FALAM TAKUN AAAYAATEAA TUTLAA A’LAYKUM FA TAKBARTUM WA KUNTUM QAWMAN MMUJREMEENA.\nBut as to those who rejected Allah, (to them will be said): “Were not Our Signs rehearsed to you? But ye were arrogant, and were a people given to sin! \nوَاِذَا قِيْلَ اِنَّ وَعْدَ اللّٰهِ حَقٌّ وَّالسَّاعَةُ لَا رَيْبَ فِيْهَا قُلْتُمْ مَّا نَدْرِىْ مَا السَّاعَةُ ۙ اِنْ نَّظُنُّ اِلَّا ظَنًّا وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِمُسْتَيْقِنِيْنَ‏(32)\nWA EZAA QEELA INNAL WA’DAL LAAHE HAQQUWN WWAALSSAAA’ATU LAA RAYBA FEEHAA IZ QULTUM MAA NADREAA MAA SAA-A’TO IN NNAZUNNU ILLAA ZANNAN WA MAA NAHNO BEMUSTAYQENEENA.\n“And when it was said that the promise of Allah was true, and that the Hour- there was no doubt about its (coming), ye used to say, 'We know not what is the hour: we only think it is an idea, and we have no firm assurance.'“ \nوَبَدَا لَهُمْ سَيِّاٰتُ مَا عَمِلُوْا وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(33)\nWABADAA LAHUM SAYAAATU MAA A’MELOO WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nThen will appear to them the evil (fruits) of what they did, and they will be completely encircled by that which they used to mock at! \nوَقِيْلَ الْيَوْمَ نَنْسٰٮكُمْ كَمَا نَسِيْتُمْ لِقَآءَ يَوْمِكُمْ هٰذَا وَمَاْوٰٮكُمُ النَّارُ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ نّٰصِرِيْنَ‏(34)\nWA QEELAD YAWMA NANSAAKUM KAMAA NASEETUM LE-QAAA-AL YAWMEKUM HAAZAA WAMAAWAAKUMU TAMASSANAN WA MAA LAKUM MIN NAASEREEN.\nIt will also be said: “This Day We will forget you as ye forgot the meeting of this Day of yours! and your abode is the Fire, and no helpers have ye! \nذٰلِكُمْ بِاَنَّكُمُ اتَّخَذْتُمْ اٰيٰتِ اللّٰهِ هُزُوًا وَّغَرَّتْكُمُ الْحَيٰوةُ الدُّنْيَا‌ ۚ فَالْيَوْمَ لَا يُخْرَجُوْنَ مِنْهَا وَلَا هُمْ يُسْتَعْتَبُوْنَ‏(35)\nZAALEKUM BEAANNAKUMU TAKHAZTUM AAYAATIL LAAHE HOZOWANW WWAGHARRATKUMU HAYAATUD DUNYAA FALYAWMA LAA YUKHRAJOONA MINHAA WA LAA HUM HUM YUSTA’TABOON.\n“This, because ye used to take the Signs of Allah in jest, and the life of the world deceived you:” (From) that Day, therefore, they shall not be taken out thence, nor shall they be received into Grace. \nفَلِلّٰهِ الْحَمْدُ رَبِّ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَرَبِّ الْاَرْضِ رَبِّ الْعٰلَمِيْنَ‏(36)\nFALILLAAHE HAMDO RABBE SAMAAWAATE WA RABBE ARZE RABBE A’ALAMEEN.\nThen Praise be to Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, Lord and Cherisher of all the Worlds! \nوَلَهُ الْكِبْرِيَآءُ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ‌ وَهُوَ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(37)\nLAHUL AL-KEBREEAAAU FIL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA HOWA A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nTo Him be glory throughout the heavens and the earth: and He is Exalted in Power, Full of Wisdom! ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Jaaseyah (The Kneeling)\nThere are 37 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. This Surah is also called Surah al-Shari’ah. It is narrated that whoever recites this Surah will not be frightened on the Day of Judgement and his private parts will remain covered (whereas all people will be raised naked on this day).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah will not see Jahannam and neither will he hear the voice of its flames. Keeping this Surah in one’s possession makes him a beloved of the people and protects him from tyrant rulers. It also keeps one safe from those who love to slander and backbite. If it is placed on the neck of a newborn child, it ensures safety and protection from all calamities."
